{
  "$schema": "http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#",
  "$id": "my_card_scores.schema.json",
  "title": "Graded MY PARLAYS cards (R87) - data/my_card_scores.json",
  "description": "The LOCKED cards recorded in data/my_cards/ resolved: prop legs against nflverse stats_player_week yards (hit = yards >= the recorded line), game legs against FINAL results when a finals source is reachable (`finals_source` names which, or that none was). Per week: the counts, the five outcome buckets, and the record per dial and per leg count - hit rate, mean conviction, log-loss and Brier of the recorded model against whether the whole card hit, plus a display-only $100 flat stake. HONESTY: weeks_resolved 0 is a valid document that says so (`skipped`) with null metrics; an unresolved leg is pending, never a miss; with nothing graded every metric is null, never 0. `cards[]` holds the GRADED cards - the complete record of what was offered is data/my_cards/. Written by scripts/resolve_my_cards.py; read by app/views/myparlays.js (the RECORD line). Optional feed.",
